{"author":{"id":"74d00943840c076a36c3dd4814646ad6086474ee541c0a42f825b943c847a718"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1542049481,"nonce":"z/IsqLpXqSuwMmBXX0qq0+iTTvU=","metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNzk5Mzg5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/72#issuecomment-437993890"},"message":"Eh, \"priority\" and/or \"severity\" are quite common for \"real\" bug trackers, e.g. [bugzilla](https://www.bugzilla.org/) or [mantis](http://www.mantisbt.org/). Priority usually expresses the importance of getting a bug fixes/an issue closed, often from the maintainer's point of view. Severity expresses the impact of a bug/issue (e.g. is it only inconvenient, does the application crash or does it corrupt data). Both are often used for sorting issues and deciding what to tackle next.\n\nOT: there are alternatives to maintainer-/user-set priority, e.g. \"[user pain](http://www.lostgarden.com/2008/05/improving-bug-triage-with-user-pain.html)\".","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1542049544,"nonce":"My6Y7gMdQGP1jN1GkOHp6pkyHlY=","metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE1MDc0OTQ4MA=="},"target":"87453f33d7a88b38da514685f08841337adfbd9bfeec8eb996900ceb8bd650cf","message":"Er, \"priority\" and/or \"severity\" are quite common for \"real\" bug trackers, e.g. [bugzilla](https://www.bugzilla.org/) or [mantis](http://www.mantisbt.org/). Priority usually expresses the importance of getting a bug fixes/an issue closed, often from the maintainer's point of view. Severity expresses the impact of a bug/issue (e.g. is it only inconvenient, does the application crash or does it corrupt data). Both are often used for sorting issues and deciding what to tackle next.\n\nOT: there are alternatives to maintainer-/user-set priority, e.g. \"[user pain](http://www.lostgarden.com/2008/05/improving-bug-triage-with-user-pain.html)\".","files":null}]}